# Cadences — a line of Spw as a loop, and each character's way of playing it
# A design, proposed. book/scripts/modules/spw-cadence.mjs reads and plays it; the desk shows it behind the land-answers trial.
#>lore_land_surfaces_cadences
#:surface #!proposal
#:operation #!prime
#:fixity #!experimental
#:layer #!pragmatics

~<rationale>{
  A line of Spw already has a rhythm: signs that strike, containers that hold, words with syllables. Read as time, the line is a score, and anyone who writes one has written a loop. Each character then plays the same loop the way they live, so a reader hears who someone is before anyone says a word, and a line written at the desk becomes something to keep, pass along and change. That is the reason to wonder twice: as a player, what this line will do in the hands of another; as an artist, what line to write next.
}

^"sigils"{
  bang: "! an accent on the beat"
  probe: "? a rest that asks, then a pickup"
  potential: "~ a tie: the last note sustains"
  confluence: "& a chord: two voices at once"
  value: "* a repeat, or a named sample struck twice"
  integration: "^ the line rises, and stays risen"
  ground: ". the ground note, in the bass, and the pitch comes home"
  config: "= swing: a lean on the off-beat"
  measure: "% a bar line; %3 sets three beats to the bar"
  annotation: "# a mark, struck like a written accent"
  perspective: "@ a solo voice, an octave up; @name also says who plays it"
  substrate: "$ the material sets the timbre: glass, frost, flour, berry, oak, ink, brass, steam"
}

^"containers"{
  frame: "[ ] its items fill one bar, and the first is the one chosen, accented"
  body: "{ } a loop, played twice"
  grouping: "( ) a tuplet, inside one beat"
  capsule: "< > call, and a softer response a step down"
  words: "a word sets syllables: each vowel group is a hit inside its beat, and its vowel sets the note (a e i o u y)"
}

^"players"{
  boof: "steady on the half beat; a question lands on the downbeat, nose first. From her temperament: unhurried until she is not"
  ants: "every note split in two, the second a step up, passed along the line. From the torch-ants: torch to torch"
  genie: "swung, and priced: each accent is paid for with the next plain note, which becomes a rest. From his weight: the price of every granted thing"
  bane: "every accent a beat early, announced, and so it comes. From his line: what he announces comes true"
  boon: "every note a chord and held to the next; nothing cut short. From his line: never smaller"
  bonewap: "exact, no swing, every beat said, softly where the line had nothing. From its weight: only what the frame will bear, declared"
  porter: "one broad note a beat at most, the weight on the first of the bar and its middle. From his temperament: steady as a sack of flour"
  clerk: "quick and short, on the sixteenth, a tally struck at the end of each bar. From the slips: a line for the cause"
  clown: "every note big, the downbeats biggest, each sliding up into place. From the clown: big feelings"
  mime: "one note a bar at most, in the minor, the rest silence; the minor is the cue the mimes already have"
  figure: "unvoiced. Nobody has said"
}

^"joins"{
  desk: "with the land-answers trial on, a line the land answers also shows its ring, in the time of whoever it names with @ (else Boof), heard only when pressed, and in anyone else's time on request; the line travels as /scriptorium/?cast=…"
  portraits: "signatureRing(id) draws a character's own line (characters.mjs identitySpell) as a ring around their portrait"
  lanes: "proposed: a rhythm found in the lanes (pie-rhythm.mjs, pie-levels.spw) is kept as the line that plays it, so a reader can take it to the desk, play it in another character's time, change one sign, and carry it back"
  remix: "proposed: a kept line can be written over; the old line stays beside it, so a reader can see what one sign changed"
}

!guards[
  "Nothing plays on its own. Sound starts only from a press, at a gentle level, at most twice round"
  "No character is given words. A cadence is how they play, never what they say"
  "The figure stays unvoiced"
  "Reduced motion stills the ring; the sound is unaffected"
]

?open[
  "Should a found rhythm in the lanes become a line kept on the reader's shelf, and where is that shelf"
  "Should the cast pages show each character's signature ring"
  "Should a line's tempo be its own (a %tempo term) or the room's"
  "Does the figure ever get a cadence, and who decides when"
]
